WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
 Hey, Marvel fans.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.580
I'm joined by Sarah Finn.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:03.570
How are you doing?
- Hello.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.370
I'm great.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.770
It's very exciting
to be here tonight.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:06.660
How are you?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.050
 I'm-- I'm speechless.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.200
This is incredible.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.210
What has it been like to
see these young adults

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.100
that you cast grow into the
characters that they are now?

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.900
 Yeah, it's a little
emotional, isn't

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.790
it, to think about the journey.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.030
And when we first cast Tom,
and Zendaya, and Jacob,

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.580
I think Jacob's screen test
was his first time he ever

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.530
set foot on a set in his life.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.420
And now to see how
far they've come

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.380
and have the end of
the trilogy here,

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.690
I'm very excited
to see the movie.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:34.670
I haven't seen it yet.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.040
I'm very excited to see it
and to see how the fans react.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.500
 Well, you've done an
incredible job at casting.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.710
Like, it's this-- kudos to you.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.660
What was it like
bringing back characters

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.730
like Willem and Alfred?

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.180
 Am I allowed to
talk about that?

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.110
I don't think so, Megan.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:50.910
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.890
 I mean, it was in the trailer.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.120
Come on, Sarah.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.230
I think you can.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.390
 Yeah, it's bonkers.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.300
It's-- this movie is as big
as anything we've ever done.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.780
And it's really exciting to
see how they're all going

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.280
to interact on screen together.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.650
 Did you ever think
that would happen?

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.450
 No.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:08.500
No, I didn't.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.300
I didn't.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.800
When I first heard the
idea for the movie,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.150
I thought, this is impossible.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.410
But--

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.880
 But here we are.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.980
Here we are.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.960
Was there a moment where
you're like, I don't

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.400
know if we can pull this off?

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.570
This is so big.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.620
This is the biggest
Spider-Man film yet.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.420
 Yes.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.820
Luckily, on my end,
a lot of the cast

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.400
was already in existence
that I had cast

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.170
and from other wonderful
casting directors

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.030
who worked on this film
in much earlier versions.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.880
So in terms of
pulling it off, I'm

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.430
going to toss that ball to the
incredible production people,

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:41.190
our producers Amy,
Rachel, Kevin Feige, Jon

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.530
Watts, everyone who
worked so hard to pull

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.640
off a movie on this scale.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.690
[MUSIC PLAYING]

